# Egeria-smart-collections
# Demonstrates the Smart Collections Integration Connector.  It creates a Results Set collection and a Saved Query
# asset, links them together with a SmartQuery relationship, attaches the results set to the Smart Collections
# Integration Connector as a catalog target, and then asks the connector to refresh.  Once the refresh has run, the
# results set's membership will match the elements returned by the saved query, and its createdTime/startTime/
# completionTime/completionMessage properties will have been updated.
# https://egeria-project.org/concepts/collection

@baseURL=https://localhost:7443
@viewServer=view-server

###
# =====================================================================================================================
# Manage the authentication token.  Run this request to create/refresh the token.

# @name Token (RequestBody)
POST {{baseURL}}/api/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId" : "peterprofile",
  "password" : "secret"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body); %}


###
# =====================================================================================================================
# Step 1: Create the Results Set collection.  Its membership will be maintained by the Smart Collections Integration
# Connector, based on the saved query linked to it in step 3.
# https://egeria-project.org/concepts/collection

# @name createResultsSet
POST {{baseURL}}/servers/{{viewServer}}/api/open-metadata/collection-manager/collections
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "class" : "NewElementRequestBody",
  "isOwnAnchor" : true,
  "properties": {
    "class" : "ResultsSetProperties",
    "qualifiedName": "ResultsSet::IntegrationConnectors",
    "displayName" : "Integration Connectors Results Set",
    "description" : "Membership is maintained by the Smart Collections Integration Connector from the attached saved query."
  }
}

> {% client.global.set("resultsSetGUID", response.body.guid); %}


###
# =====================================================================================================================
# Step 2: Create the Saved Query asset that defines the REST call used to work out the results set's membership.
# This example searches the open metadata ecosystem for integration connectors.
# https://egeria-project.org/concepts/asset

# @name createSavedQuery
POST {{baseURL}}/servers/{{viewServer}}/api/open-metadata/asset-maker/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "class" : "NewElementRequestBody",
  "isOwnAnchor" : true,
  "properties": {
    "class" : "SavedQueryProperties",
    "qualifiedName": "SavedQuery::IntegrationConnectors",
    "displayName" : "Find Integration Connectors",
    "description" : "Searches the open metadata ecosystem for integration connector elements.",
    "queryURL" : "https://localhost:7443/servers/view-server/api/open-metadata/metadata-expert/metadata-elements/by-search-string",
    "queryRequestBody" : "{\"class\":\"SearchStringRequestBody\",\"searchString\":\"Integration\",\"startsWith\":false,\"endsWith\":false,\"ignoreCase\":true,\"metadataElementTypeName\":\"IntegrationConnector\"}"
  }
}

> {% client.global.set("savedQueryGUID", response.body.guid); %}


###
# =====================================================================================================================
# Step 3: Link the results set to the saved query using the new attachSmartQuery operation (SmartQuery relationship, 0725).

# @name attachSmartQuery
POST {{baseURL}}/servers/{{viewServer}}/api/open-metadata/collection-manager/collections/results-sets/{{resultsSetGUID}}/smart-query/{{savedQueryGUID}}/attach
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "class" : "NewRelationshipRequestBody",
  "properties": {
    "class": "SmartQueryProperties",
    "label": "Membership query",
    "description": "Determines the membership of the results set."
  }
}


###
# =====================================================================================================================
# Step 4: Attach the results set to the Smart Collections Integration Connector as a catalog target.  The connector's
# GUID is fixed by its registration in the core content pack (see IntegrationConnectorDefinition.
# SMART_COLLECTIONS_MEMBERSHIP_MANAGER).  The catalog target name matches the one recognized by the connector
# (SmartCollectionsCatalogTarget.CATALOG_TARGET).
# https://egeria-project.org/concepts/integration-connector/

@integrationConnectorGUID=217bd925-b50d-4596-9ade-1d7a940e8874

###
# @name addCatalogTarget
POST {{baseURL}}/servers/{{viewServer}}/api/open-metadata/asset-maker/integration-connectors/{{integrationConnectorGUID}}/catalog-targets/{{resultsSetGUID}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "class" : "NewRelationshipRequestBody",
  "properties": {
    "class": "CatalogTargetProperties",
    "catalogTargetName" : "resultsSetToMaintain"
  }
}


###
# =====================================================================================================================
# Step 5: Ask the nanny-daemon integration daemon to refresh the connector.  This calls the integration daemon
# directly (rather than routing through runtime-manager by server GUID) since the platform cataloguer's catalogued
# Connection for an integration daemon can point at the wrong daemon when more than one is configured - see
# https://egeria-project.org/concepts/integration-daemon/

# @name refreshConnectors
POST {{baseURL}}/servers/nanny-daemon/open-metadata/integration-daemon/integration-connectors/refresh
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "class" : "NameRequestBody",
  "name" : "SmartCollectionsMembershipManager"
}


###
# =====================================================================================================================
# Step 6: Check the outcome.  The results set's createdTime/startTime/completionTime/completionMessage properties
# should now be set, and its members should match the elements returned by the saved query.

# @name getResultsSet
POST {{baseURL}}/servers/{{viewServer}}/api/open-metadata/collection-manager/collections/{{resultsSetGUID}}/retrieve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "class" : "GetRequestBody"
}


###
# @name getResultsSetMembers
POST {{baseURL}}/servers/{{viewServer}}/api/open-metadata/collection-manager/collections/{{resultsSetGUID}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "class" : "ResultsRequestBody"
}
